{{- /*
What enrolling a tree writes for the two plugin hosts, which name the file
differently and read the same shape into it: opencode.json in a tree for
opencode, kilo.json for Kilo Code. One asset rather than two identical ones, so
a change to how the server is registered reaches both. Should the two shapes
ever diverge, split this back into a file each rather than adding a knob.

The MCP registration and the deny rules together: a tree can be enrolled on a
host where `faramir init --agent` never ran, and the enrolment is what the
operator did. The rules merge with whatever the home holds, so a rule written
twice refuses the same thing once.

Claude Code reads a different shape under a different key, and is in
claude/settings.local.json.tmpl.

GENERATED. The paths come from internal/install/protectedpaths.go, written once
and rendered into each agent's own spelling; nothing here is a path of its own.
Add one there.

Deny rules only, and no catch-all, for the reason given in permissions.json.tmpl.
read and edit take the same list: a value the agent cannot read is one it can
still destroy.
*/ -}}
{
  "mcp": {
    "faramir": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": ["{{.BinDir}}/faramir", "mcp"],
      "enabled": true
    }
  },
  "permission": {
    "read": {
{{ jsonDenyMap "      " (pluginPatterns .Layout) }}
    },
    "edit": {
{{ jsonDenyMap "      " (pluginPatterns .Layout) }}
    }
  }
}
